129 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 56 0 R
/E (Throughout history, women have never been mere spectators of the destiny of nations; more often than not, they have been the silent force that holds societies together when everything seems to be falling apart. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
130 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 56 0 R
/E (In Morocco, women have left their mark on history through their courage, intelligence, and devotion. From women who supported the resistance during the struggle for independence, carrying messages, protecting fighters, and risking their lives in the face of repression, to those who preserved the identity, traditions, and collective memory of their people, Moroccan women have contributed to shaping the destiny of their nation. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
131 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 56 0 R
/E (Others have challenged the barriers of their time, opening doors to education, science, and freedom for future generations. Yet, how many of these women have had their names engraved in history books? How many have changed the course of events without ever receiving the recognition they deserved? For centuries, history has celebrated the victories of men without always acknowledging the hands of women that helped make them possible. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
132 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 56 0 R
/E (THE SILENT ARCHITECTS OF HISTORY)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
